      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GANDHI MAIL (10) had to work to get to the front in the Bill Collins Sprint at Melton last start and while he couldn't see it out he boxed on solidly for fifth. Won twice in a row here prior and although a wide draw presents a challenge he has enough early speed to get across from there. YOUR MAJESTY (5) made an encouraging return when she raced three wide without cover but fought well for a 1.7m last week. Should be fitter for that and is suited up to a distance where she has won five of eight attempts. LONDON TO A BRICK (9) hasn't raced since the Brisbane winter carnival but has been readied with three trials, winning the latest. His best is good enough to win this. PESCO POLLO (6) comes off a solid effort to place last week and is a four-time winner at the longer distance.",
